{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 998244353L;\n    static long[] fact;\n    static long[] invFact;\n\n    static long pow(long a, long e) {\n        long r = 1;\n        while (e > 0) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) r = r * a % MOD;\n            a = a * a % MOD;\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    static void prepare(int max) {\n        fact = new long[max + 1];\n        invFact = new long[max + 1];\n        fact[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= max; i++) fact[i] = fact[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n        invFact[max] = pow(fact[max], MOD - 2);\n        for (int i = max; i >= 1; i--) invFact[i - 1] = invFact[i] * i % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static long ncr(int n, int r) {\n        if (r < 0 || r > n) return 0;\n        return fact[n] * invFact[r] % MOD * invFact[n - r] % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static long invNcr(int n, int r) {\n        if (r < 0 || r > n) return 0;\n        return fact[r] * fact[n - r] % MOD * invFact[n] % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static long smallInv(int x) {\n        return invFact[x] * fact[x - 1] % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static long add(long a, long b) {\n        long v = a + b;\n        return v >= MOD ? v - MOD : v;\n    }\n\n    static long sub(long a, long b) {\n        long v = a - b;\n        return v < 0 ? v + MOD : v;\n    }\n\n    static long mul(long a, long b) {\n        return a * b % MOD;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int m = sc.nextInt();\n\n        prepare(n + m);\n\n        long phaseSize = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\n            long pi = mul(ncr(n, i), invNcr(n + m, i));\n            phaseSize = add(phaseSize, pi);\n        }\n\n        long answer = 0;\n        for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {\n            long numPhases = mul(m + k, smallInv(k));\n            long term = mul(ncr(n, k), mul(numPhases, phaseSize));\n            if ((k & 1) == 1) answer = add(answer, term);\n            else answer = sub(answer, term);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(answer);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef pow_mod(a, e):\n    r = 1\n    while e > 0:\n        if e & 1:\n            r = r * a % MOD\n        a = a * a % MOD\n        e >>= 1\n    return r\n\ndef prepare(max_val):\n    global fact, invFact\n    fact = [1] * (max_val + 1)\n    invFact = [1] * (max_val + 1)\n    for i in range(1, max_val + 1):\n        fact[i] = fact[i-1] * i % MOD\n    invFact[max_val] = pow_mod(fact[max_val], MOD - 2)\n    for i in range(max_val, 0, -1):\n        invFact[i-1] = invFact[i] * i % MOD\n\ndef ncr(n, r):\n    if r < 0 or r > n:\n        return 0\n    return fact[n] * invFact[r] % MOD * invFact[n - r] % MOD\n\ndef invNcr(n, r):\n    if r < 0 or r > n:\n        return 0\n    return fact[r] * fact[n - r] % MOD * invFact[n] % MOD\n\ndef smallInv(x):\n    return invFact[x] * fact[x-1] 